# Fuss {2}{R/W}: "each attacking creature you control" -- on Bot2's turn 4 Bot2's Memnite attacks and Bot1's Ornithopter stays untapped
# at home (it is not attacking). Bot1 casts Fuss (Mox Pearl pays the hybrid white-or-red symbol; Mox Emerald and Mox Jet the generic) in Bot2's declare attackers step: no creature of Bot1's is
# attacking and Bot2's attacker is not Bot1's, so nothing gets a counter: Memnite is still 1/1, Ornithopter 0/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fuss // Bother
Ornithopter
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Memnite)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fuss // Bother.Cast(Ability: Fuss)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Fuss // Bother
Stack.Count = 0
